  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Framed Working Sheet",
    "overview": "A pale frame surrounds a white working sheet. TikTok Sans, teal ink, quiet borders, and recognizable product imagery extend the established Columbia / KRYGA visual world into a compact owner-facing interface. The hierarchy favors a clear current state, readable choices, and an explicit action.\n\nThis is a scan of the implemented `/admin` surface, not a redesign or a complete token inventory of either storefront. The frontmatter records admin values from `src/admin/admin.css`, including its final cascade overrides; component structure comes from `src/admin/Admin.jsx`. The existing storefronts retain their own visual authority in `src/styles.css` and `columbia-site/src/styles.css`. Their shared type family, cold-paper surfaces, and distinct teal / navy identities inform this extension. The framing metaphor describes the established admin brief; it does not establish a new brand identity.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A pale outer frame and white working sheet, separated by quiet borders.",
      "One type family with compact, sentence-case labels and restrained weight changes.",
      "Teal for selection and the primary action; blue for keyboard focus.",
      "Real storefront imagery that keeps Columbia and KRYGA recognizable.",
